    "isActive": true,
    "version": 9,
    "baseScale": 1,
    "name": "[2] Bizzer Swarm",
    "sheetData": {
      "notes": [
        {
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "communication",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Bizzers have no\nmeans of communicating to other\ncreatures, unless you count their\nincessant buzzing.",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Communication",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "zVjSfIr9c1OUqV7imIzb"
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "kBywmo3EdxTgn60sDcjV",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "originId": "customization",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "description": "Certain Swarms may\ninflict an Ailment in addition\nto hindering magic use when they use\ntheir Engulf Ability.",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null
        },
        {
          "description": "Bizzer Swarms make their\nnests in mana-rich environments, for\nexample wizarding structures or\nmagical biomes. They are infamous\nfor causing injuries, and even a few\nfatalities, at Shard’s University and its\nrival school in the Galvanus Peninsula,\nby showing up during an important\nmagical demonstration or eating the\nflight spell of a commuting professor.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "habitat",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "id": "3m3jq88w2MTTMDF8ChOi",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat"
        },
        {
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Rusty imbued items, a\nsingle Bizzer moving along a wall,\nthat horrible buzzing noise.",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "id": "BLqk4C5Il8xU6u4P7zMR",
          "name": "Indicators",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "id": "4zmwofqIGoKFfLDseJTM",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "description": "Buzz, buzz buzz.\nBuzz buzz!",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "role-playing-notes"
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "UgwsmgmWqAKnoWbw9yc3",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "tactics",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Bizzers are instinctual\ncreatures and don’t formulate\ncombat strategies.\n\nHowever, soldiers and bandits have\nbeen known to weaponize them for\nuse against arcane foes. Buzz Bombs,\nglass jars filled with Bizzers, are very\npopular among raiders in particular."
        }
      ],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "hl4JMmBdBRRKDQjDUzyI",
          "description": "*The Bizzer Swarm is not a single entity, it is made up of hundreds of tiny bugs.*\n\n- Bizzer Swarms can only be hit by Attacks made with large, broad objects or that target the entire Battlefield Area the swarm occupies. Your GM will decide which objects or strikes will make a significant impact on the swarm. Other Attacks will only kill a handful of bugs, and wont impact the effectiveness of the swarm.\n- Bizzer Swarms are immune to Ailments. A few of the bugs may be affected, but not enough to incapacitate the swarm as a whole.\n- Bizzers can fly and their Speed Rating is Fast.\n- If the Bizzer Swarm is reduced to 0 Hearts, the swarm has been killed or reduced to a harmless volume.",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "buzzing-mass",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Buzzing Mass ",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": ""
        },
        {
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "description": "*Bizzer Swarms surround a target and drain away any mana on or around them. A hungry swarm is noisy and incessant.*\n\n- Engulfing a foe requires the Bizzer Swarm to use its Action, but does not require an Attack roll.\n- Engulf can be used on a single creature or object in the same Area as the swarm. Bizzers only target creatures or items with Magical Abilities. They have no interest in non-magical entities.\n- The target is unable to use any Magical Abilities while engulfed by the Bizzer Swarm.\n- Anyone attacking the Swarm while it is using this Ability will hit the swarms target instead on an unsuccessful attempt.\n- The Swarm will do its best to follow its target, but will abandon pursuit if it becomes hazardous for the swarm, such as the target getting too close to flames or being submerged in liquid.\n- If the target somehow escapes the Swarm, they remain unable to use any magical Abilities for 1 Turn.",
          "id": "NFig5RXLzrlOvcsBUtbU",
          "subtext": "",
          "counters": {},
          "name": "Engulf [B]",
          "value": 0,
          "originId": "engulf-b",
          "counterOverrides": {}
        }
      ],
