          "name": "Communication"
        },
        {
          "name": "Customization",
          "value": 0,
          "id": "TbmqEj5EUEctOhC2HNHh",
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "customization",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Mushdooms take well to certain Champion Abilities, having the appropriate amount of strength if lacking in true courage.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "id": "EkmveCKOYamj0zXWyGkU",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "description": "Air thick with inert telepathic spores, enormous circular footprints in the ground, emboldened and aggressive groups of funguys in the area.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Mushdooms are nasty bullies at their core. Even if not communicating directly with someone, they loom with aggressive body language and open hostility. Naturally, if something noticeably bigger or stronger confronts them they quickly revert to meeker habits.",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "Te6J8fsl5dbWGbjFHrtV"
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "id": "1IaJuknUGmIsIElaETPo",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "description": "Mushdooms like to bully and overwhelm opponents. A favored trick is to knock over an enemy with their punch and then have Funguy minions swarm them for a pin or a finish.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null
        }
      ],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "UBn9bdVG3pISRPCIRbk1",
          "description": "The Mushdoom is Large and has Supernatural Might\n\nThe Mushdoom’s body is oddly tough, and they are considered to be wearing Medium Armor.",
          "counters": {},
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Not so Tiny Toadstool"
        },
        {
          "description": "> Funguys do not speak in any conventional way. They instead communicate by passing thoughts to and from their spores. This allows seamless communication with their allies, but is often disorienting and confusing for the uninitiated.\n\nA Funguy may take a Turn to release their Telepathic Spores, affecting all within adjacent Areas.. This allows all the Funguy within this Area to mentally communicate for the remainder of the conflict.\n\nAny non-Funguy within this Area must make a Grit Check. Failure means that the sudden influx of foreign thoughts is a bit much for the target to handle and they are afflicted with the Disoriented Status Ailment for the remainder of the conflict. \n\nSuccess means they are able to understand the funguy’s thoughts (as well as any other non-funguy in the area that succeeded on their Check) and even communicate with them telepathically. They also receive an Edge on any further Grit Checks called on by this Ability.\n\nCertain things might blow or wash away the spores at the Game Master’s discretion. This ends the Ability’s effect immediately.\n\nFurther use of this Ability on the same Targets within the same conflict have no effect, unless the spores were blown or washed away. \n\nSynthetic Creatures (such as Bio-Mechanoids) are entirely immune to this Ability.\n\nIf this Ability is used outside of combat, one can assume that its effects last for a few minutes or so.",
          "id": "LMDBEiFNZghv4urbX6EQ",
          "modifiers": [],
          "name": "Telepathic Spores",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "name": "Fist of the Fungus MkII",
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "description": "> Mushdoom’s eschew the swift fighting style of their smaller brethren in favor of raw brutality.\n\nThe Mushdoom makes unarmed attacks as if wielding a Mighty Weapon.\n\nIn addition, anyone of normal size or smaller that is struck by the Mushdoom must succeed on a Grit Check or become Toppled.\n\n",
          "id": "TojSzVGX1Cv8Sv4hFqlf"
        }
      ]
    },
