        },
        {
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "id": "uiQYCtKfmsd63LFLsITH",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "name": "Customization",
          "value": 0,
          "description": "Proudhound breeds\nalso come in Small (Puggoe) and\nLarge (Bernord) varieties. Each clan is\nknown for having a different Mighty\nCombination Weapon as their\nsignature Packsword. Note, Small\nProudhounds can still use their\nPacksword without penalty.",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "habitat",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Most common around the\nPride Coast, their ancestral\nhomeland, Proudhounds travel far\nand wide in search of worthy foes.",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "Y0cPHOiVN2FPgDKtwcj1"
        },
        {
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "A wistful howl in the wind,\nheavy paw prints, corpses with large\nslash wounds.",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "indicators",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "NeBaTBjqd6mE8rQoF567",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Indicators"
        },
        {
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Proudhounds\nare dignified mercenaries and are\noccasionally too honest for such a\nprofession. They are tremendously\nloyal, and are unlikely to betray\nfriends or employers.",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "id": "a69hdtvaqGncfv6OW55m",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Proudhounds abhor deception and other tricks and will:\n- Seek a head-to-head fight whenever practical.\n- Target challenging or skilled warriors first.\n- Use Canine Pounce to quickly dispatch a weakened adversary.",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "Fcxa9AbWTzrXMGaHBGeb"
        }
      ],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "originId": "canine-pounce-a",
          "type": null,
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "subtext": "",
          "counters": {},
          "description": "*Proudhounds can bound into battle.*\n\n- Proudhounds have Supernatural Leaping (p107).\n- **Leap Attack:** After leaping, Proudhounds can use their Action to deliver a shuddering blow that:\n  - Gains a +2 to hit.\n  - Does +1 Heart of Damage.\n  - Drains 1 Heart from the Proudhound whether the Attack lands or not.",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "name": "Canine Pounce [A]",
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "id": "50kTJDvoglgW467fGRR8",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": "",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Doggone Good Sense ",
          "originId": "doggone-good-sense",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "aLKWG8qsTAGkSnUTRxHr",
          "description": "*Mundymutts hear and smell better than any other species in the Outer World.*\n\n- Mange have an Edge on all Insight Checks and Contests involving hearing or sense of smell. For example, tracking or sniffing out a hidden or disguised individual.\n- Mange can smell mana and can tell when magic of any kind is being used, or was recently used, nearby. They can even discern between Bright and Dark mana.\n- Things not native to Outer World (Dimensional Strays, Asuras, Devas, etc.) smell off and make them uneasy. This could explain their infamous dislike of the Rai-Neko."
        },
        {
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "*An especially intimidating bark.*\n\nOnce per Fight the Proudhound can use their Turn to snarl and bark in an attempt to scare adversaries within a range of 1 Battlefield Area.\n\n**Requires a Grit Contest**\n- **Success:** You are Terrified (p271) until the Proudhound is dealt with.",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": "",
          "originId": "fearsome-growl-b",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": null,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "ued4JVNrBO5SPspE0KQD",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Fearsome Growl [B]"
        }
      ],
