      },
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "JvTv62FsdIQ7t82Pig1c",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Caustic Miasma ",
          "description": "*The Shadow Beast is followed by a fog of malignantly charged Dark Mana that eats away at flesh, steel, and bone.*\n\n- Any Area the Shadow Beast occupies gains the Harmful Battlefield Condition (p250). The Shadow Beast itself is immune to this effect.\n- Long exposure to this Ability may damage structures and unattended objects at the GMs discretion.\n- This Ability is negated by the presence of a Star Gem, or other form of sunlight, emanating from a source up to one Battlefield Area away from the Shadow Beast.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": null,
          "originId": "caustic-miasma",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "AJhX5B1BZeaEvADHfYBX",
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "name": "Forsaken Shadow ",
          "value": 0,
          "description": "*Shadow Beasts fear light, knowing instinctively that it is their only real weakness. Darkness, no matter how malicious, only comforts them.*\n\n- If the Shadow Beast comes within 2 Battlefield Areas of a Star Gem, or other source of sunlight, it is automatically Terrified (p271). The Beast will retreat from the source if at all possible.\n- Attacks inflicting Bright Damage receive a +1 Damage bonus against the Shadow Beast.\n- Attacks inflicting Dark Damage do not harm the Shadow Beast, and will actually restore 1 lost Heart.\n- Light from a mundane source, such as a lantern or torch, only serves to aggravate the Shadow Beast. They know it is only a pale imitation of what they truly fear.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "type": null,
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "forsaken-shadow",
          "subtext": "",
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "neJ08UFntFldrDI5TyVR",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Howls Of The Lost [B]",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "*Faces contorted in fear and woe ebb and flow along the surface of the Shadow Beast, emitting pitiful cries as they surface and submerge. Hear them and despair.*\n\nIf you come within 1 Battlefield Area of the Shadow Beast, you must attempt to resist its horror.\n\n**You require a Grit Check**\n- **Failure:** You contract the Dispirited Ailment (p269). The Ailment lasts until the Shadow Beast has left your sight.\n- **Success:** You are immune to this Ability for 24 hours.\n\nAdds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": "",
          "originId": "howls-of-the-lost-b",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": null
        },
        {
          "id": "nwIPEYmV2dD9nMfVIsYQ",
          "description": "*The Shadow Beast's body moves like liquid darkness, yet remains concrete.*\n\n- The Shadow Beast is Fast.\n- +6 Defense Rating, the Shadow Beasts density repels weak Attacks.\n- The Shadow Beast is able to climb sheer surfaces with lease, and is unhindered by the Isolated Battlefield Condition.",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "surging-darkness-b",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Surging Darkness [B]",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": ""
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": "",
          "originId": "tragic-behemoth",
          "type": null,
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "*Even though their shape is in constant flux, a Shadow Beast is always frightfully large.*\n\n- Shadow Beasts are Massive (p434).\n- **Sweep Attack:** Long neck and limbs strike as Arc Weapons.\n- **Focus Attack:** Stomps and bites strike as Mighty Weapons.",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Tragic Behemoth ",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "LowKJlYiP9ZztnncoxcV"
        }
      ],
