      },
      "abilities": [
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Tiny Toadstool ",
          "counters": {},
          "id": "d2rzBjilFQOnlnTCiZkk",
          "description": "> Funguy aren’t particularly tall, barely waist level to the average human (and this is even with their mushroom caps).\n\nFunguys are Small\n\nFunguys breathe and eat, though not in the same way that other humanoids do. They just sort of absorb liquids and organic matter into their body along with air. \n\nConsumables (such as potions or magical food) still affect them like they would another applicable creature, it just looks really odd.\n\nFunguys are also able to consume spoiled or unprepared organic material as Rations.\n\n",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "9kwrZc0mCo0piitFXQg9",
          "description": "> Funguys do not speak in any conventional way. They instead communicate by passing thoughts to and from their spores. This allows seamless communication with their allies, but is often disorienting and confusing for the uninitiated.\n\nA Funguy may take a Turn to release their Telepathic Spores in the Area they currently occupy. This allows all the Funguy within this Area to mentally communicate for the remainder of the conflict.\n\nAny non-Funguy within this Area must make a Grit Check. Failure means that the sudden influx of foreign thoughts is a bit much for the target to handle and they are afflicted with the Disoriented Status Ailment for the remainder of the conflict. \n\nSuccess means they are able to understand the funguy’s thoughts (as well as any other non-funguy in the area that succeeded on their Check) and even communicate with them telepathically. They also receive an Edge on any further Grit Checks called on by this Ability.\n\nCertain things might blow or wash away the spores at the Game Master’s discretion. This ends the Ability’s effect immediately.\n\nFurther use of this Ability on the same Targets within the same conflict have no effect, unless the spores were blown or washed away. \n\nSynthetic Creatures (such as Bio-Mechanoids) are entirely immune to this Ability.\n\nIf this Ability is used outside of combat, one can assume that its effects last for a few minutes or so.",
          "counters": {},
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Telepathy Spores"
        },
        {
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "1WnIxJnYh6Izvrcunm9k",
          "description": "> Most Funguy are well versed in a strange martial art that takes advantage of their small size and flexibility.\n\nThe Funguy makes Unarmed Attacks as if wielding a Quick Weapon.",
          "counters": {},
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Fist of the Fungus"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "id": "Twj5ObVjgpD46acKSX3y",
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "name": "Communication",
          "value": 0,
          "description": "Funguys are usually only capable of communicating with their Telepathy Spores, which can be a real hindrance. They utilize the signed component of low speech use when dealing with other species in a pinch.",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "originId": "communication",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "description": "Some Funguys learn Dark Aligned Sage Abilities. They have distinctly purple mushroom caps.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "customization",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {},
          "id": "DqE568jJmpxxBS0JYkYy",
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "name": "Customization",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "id": "VyFecmXdCkprqf4gZ4Fo",
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "Funguys have a preference for cold, wet places. Their favored region is the Wistful Dark (particularly the Murk) but they can also be found in thick forests or dank caves throughout the Outer World.",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null,
          "originId": "habitat",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts"
        },
        {
          "name": "Indicators",
          "value": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "id": "qK4wjk4NsFBploKEqGDl",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "starValue": null,
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "description": "A disconcerting amount of mushrooms, the sounds of very organized shuffling, a strange odor."
        },
        {
          "description": "Funguys find the strange physical excesses and constant babbling of other humanoids to be nearly intolerable. They are generally pretty grumpy dealing with them as a result.\n\nWhile there is the occasional Funguy who is curious about non-mushroom forms of sentient life, they are considered oddballs by their fellows.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "subtext": null,
          "counters": {},
          "id": "irCOXWHuITpDQD6zPTs6",
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "SEYWyZsj1nVNYWk8oGWc",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "bonus": 0,
          "valuePrefix": null,
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "description": "Funguy generally weaponise their Spores against shaky or easily confused foes. Combined efforts and assault assists are favored when fighting against stronger adversaries.",
          "valueSuffix": null,
          "starValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "subtext": null
        }
      ]
